-# Offcanvas help drawer for problems/edit, using the shared help-drawer chrome
-# (app/views/shared/_help_drawer.html.haml). Triggered by the Help (?) button
-# in the edit-page header. Body is a Bootstrap accordion (one section open at a
-# time) so the drawer opens short instead of one long scroll — collapse is
-# driven by Bootstrap's data-API, so it needs no init-ui-component wrapper and
-# survives Turbo-frame reloads on its own. Keep sections short and link out to
-# the wiki for deep reference rather than duplicating it.
= render layout: 'shared/help_drawer', locals: { id: 'problem-edit-help', title: 'Problem Editor Help', subtitle: 'Quick reference for the fields and panels on this page.' } do
  .accordion.accordion-flush#problem-edit-help-acc
    -# ---- 1. Detail card fields (open by default) ----
    .accordion-item
      %h2.accordion-header
        %button.accordion-button{type: 'button', data: {bs_toggle: 'collapse', bs_target: '#peh-detail'}, 'aria-expanded': 'true', 'aria-controls': 'peh-detail'} Detail card fields
      #peh-detail.accordion-collapse.collapse.show{data: {bs_parent: '#problem-edit-help-acc'}}
        .accordion-body
          %dl.row.small.mb-0
            %dt.col-4.fw-semibold Full name
            %dd.col-8.text-secondary Human-readable title shown to students. Required.
            %dt.col-4.fw-semibold Name
            %dd.col-8.text-secondary
              Short identifier used in filenames and the engine. Must be
              %strong unique
              and stable — renaming may break links and imports.
            %dt.col-4.fw-semibold Description
            %dd.col-8.text-secondary
              Markdown source used internally —
              %strong not shown to students directly.
              Two uses: (a) auto-generates the downloadable PDF statement, (b) feeds LLM-assisted hints. Optional; when present, its content should match the uploaded PDF.
            %dt.col-4.fw-semibold Time / memory limit
            %dd.col-8.text-secondary Per-test-case caps. Time in seconds, memory in MB.
            %dt.col-4.fw-semibold Tags
            %dd.col-8.text-secondary
              Free-form labels — topic/category plus AI-helper tags (kind
              %code llm_prompt
              ); only
              %code viva_conduct
              tags are excluded here (they have their own Conduct profile
              select, below). For viva exams, the rubric and model
              answers go in the
              %strong Examiner briefing
              field (Viva Exam card, right half of the edit page); an optional shared
              examiner persona can be layered on via the
              %strong Conduct profile
              select, which picks a
              %code viva_conduct
              tag. Reference material for
              the interviewer/grader lives separately under
              %strong Manage &rarr; Grounding
              and is attached to the problem via the
              %strong Grounding materials
              select further down this form.
            %dt.col-4.fw-semibold Submission filename
            %dd.col-8.text-secondary
              The on-disk filename used when the submission is written into the compile sandbox. Leave
              %strong blank
              to default to
              %code submission.<ext>
              (e.g.
              %code submission.cpp
              ). Override only when the harness or manager requires a specific filename — e.g. when a manager does
              %code #include "mySolution.cpp"
              set the override to match. Most common with
              %em with-managers
              problems.

    -# ---- 2. Compilation type ----
    .accordion-item
      %h2.accordion-header
        %button.accordion-button.collapsed{type: 'button', data: {bs_toggle: 'collapse', bs_target: '#peh-compile'}, 'aria-expanded': 'false', 'aria-controls': 'peh-compile'} Compilation type
      #peh-compile.accordion-collapse.collapse{data: {bs_parent: '#problem-edit-help-acc'}}
        .accordion-body.small.text-secondary
          How the submission is built before grading:
          %ul.ps-3.mb-0
            %li
              %strong Self contained
              — the submitted source compiles standalone. The default for most problems.
            %li
              %strong With managers
              — the submission is compiled together with one or more
              %em manager
              files attached to the dataset. Use this when students implement a function called by a fixed harness, or when there's a shared header/grader stub.
            %li
              %strong Viva Exam
              — special mode: no compilation and no test cases. The submission is an answer to an LLM-driven oral interview, graded against a rubric supplied via the problem's
              %strong Examiner briefing
              field, optionally layered with a shared
              %code viva_conduct
              tag.

    -# ---- 3. Datasets & live set ----
    .accordion-item
      %h2.accordion-header
        %button.accordion-button.collapsed{type: 'button', data: {bs_toggle: 'collapse', bs_target: '#peh-datasets'}, 'aria-expanded': 'false', 'aria-controls': 'peh-datasets'} Datasets &amp; live set
      #peh-datasets.accordion-collapse.collapse{data: {bs_parent: '#problem-edit-help-acc'}}
        .accordion-body
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-2
            A problem can have multiple datasets; exactly one is the
            %strong live dataset
            — that's what runs when a student submits. Switch the live
            dataset via the dropdown on the right.
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            Viva-exam problems don't use datasets at all — they're driven by
            the LLM tags described above.

    -# ---- 4. Scoring & evaluation ----
    .accordion-item
      %h2.accordion-header
        %button.accordion-button.collapsed{type: 'button', data: {bs_toggle: 'collapse', bs_target: '#peh-scoring'}, 'aria-expanded': 'false', 'aria-controls': 'peh-scoring'} Scoring &amp; evaluation
      #peh-scoring.accordion-collapse.collapse{data: {bs_parent: '#problem-edit-help-acc'}}
        .accordion-body
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-2
            %strong Score type
            controls how per-testcase scores aggregate into a final grade:
            %strong Sum
            (weighted sum, scaled to 100 — the default),
            %strong Group Min
            (IOI/ICPC subtask style — a group is only as strong as its
            weakest testcase), or
            %strong Raw Sum
            (literal sum, no normalization).
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-2
            %strong Evaluation type
            controls how a submission's output is judged against the
            expected answer. Built-in evaluators are
            %code default
            (diff that ignores whitespace + blank lines — most problems),
            %code exact
            (strict diff), and
            %code relative
            (token-by-token; numbers compared with tolerance). Custom
            evaluators —
            %code cafe
            ,
            %code cms
            , and
            %code cms-raw
            — run a checker file you attach to the dataset (Files tab).
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            %strong Heads up:
            the
            %code Raw Sum
            score type is designed to pair with the
            %code CMS-raw
            custom evaluator — other combinations will produce strange
            totals because non-custom evaluators only emit pass/fail per
            testcase.

    -# ---- 5. Toolbar & more ----
    .accordion-item
      %h2.accordion-header
        %button.accordion-button.collapsed{type: 'button', data: {bs_toggle: 'collapse', bs_target: '#peh-more'}, 'aria-expanded': 'false', 'aria-controls': 'peh-more'} Toolbar &amp; more
      #peh-more.accordion-collapse.collapse{data: {bs_parent: '#problem-edit-help-acc'}}
        .accordion-body
          %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-3.ps-3
            %li
              %span.mi.md-18.align-text-bottom query_stats
              %strong Statistics
              — submission counts, scores, language breakdown.
            %li
              %span.mi.md-18.align-text-bottom download
              %strong Download Archive
              — exports the problem + live dataset for backup or transfer.
            %li
              %span.mi.md-18.align-text-bottom history
              %strong Change history
              — audit log of edits to this problem, its dataset, and testcases.
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-1
            For deep reference (import format, checker scripts, manager files,
            initializer scripts), see the project wiki.
          %a.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary.d-inline-flex.align-items-center.gap-1{href: 'https://github.com/cafe-grader-team/cafe-grader-web/wiki/Adding-a-problem', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener'}
            %span.mi.md-18 open_in_new
            Wiki: Adding a problem
